          <h2 id="compare-title">Where aimm differs from other memory tools</h2>
          <p class="answer">
            Vector stores optimise for similarity, graph platforms for
            relationships. aimm optimises for what a coding assistant actually
            needs: recall that is fast, local and tied to your code — and that
            never passes off a stale fact as current.
          </p>
        </div>
        {/* The scroll container itself has to be focusable and named, or a
